**Theorem 4.4 (native coordinates and finite progress).** On the same
actual occurrence word, native tick and fee coordinates remain $n$ and
$2n$. All ARC Definition 10.1 opcode/purpose/input/constructed-storage
recurrences and original CAP event-counter interpretations remain valid.
Replacing the native tariff uses $G_U+\rho_U$; imposing it additionally
uses $2n+G_U+\rho_U$. Each finite completed flight in ARC's stated
supply/local-completion domain has finite such coordinates. No finite
total data, minimum role count, physical duration/energy or guaranteed
infinite progress follows.

Proof. Theorem 2.4 has precisely one patch per native occurrence and
preserves its input kind, opcode, purpose, constructor and receipt.
Thus it changes neither the event partition nor any native creation
count. In particular both ordinary/F receipts and all dead banks,
captures, versions, sender/mailbox/receiver copies coexist. ARC's vector
recurrence evaluated at these same successors therefore applies without
an independently optimized subtotal. Its finite source/recovery
completion supplies finitely many rows, each with a finite stencil.
The two tariff conventions differ by the original $2n$. Infinite
continuation would require continuing actual supply and pointwise local
completion, with unbounded receipts and potentially unbounded data. ∎

